Z||000000||Voytek||08-20-2001||05:23 PM||||Ok.  As I've said here and there, I had my 2.8 rebuilt and bored out to 3.1 (new pistons, machine work, cam, etc.).  Before the rebuilt, I had removed the cat about 2 years ago.  The engine always stunk like it was burning oil (I've had to add about 0.5 - 1L between changes).<BR>NOW the engine is fully rebuilt and it STILL stinks just as bad!!  AND I STILL have to add about 0.5-1L of oil between changes.  Is this normal?  Oh, the rebuilt has about 16,000 kms on it (about 10,000 miles).<P>Thanks for any info!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||starfighter007@msn.com||08-20-2001||06:22 PM||||maybe you have oil leaking from a valve cover and it is driping on to the exhaust manifold.||||reg||1
